    "https://www.bates.edu/career/": {
      "title": "Center for Purposeful WorkOpportunities and Programs",
      "description": "Center for Purposeful Work | Bates College Menu Search Admission Visit Campus Visit Virtually Student Financial Services Academics Calendar Course Catalog Resources Campus Dining Menu Events Map Alumni Alumni Directory Events Reunion Arts Athletics New Students Library News Parents & Families Strategic Planning About Us Purposeful Work College Store Community-Engaged Learning Equity & Inclusion President Sustainability Support Bates The Quad Center for Purposeful Work Opportunities and Programs Page Menu Purpose Connect Where to Find Us Staff Team Make an Appointment Student Teams Purpose and Your Club PW Weekly Newsletters For Alumni and Parents In The News Media Professionals Media Inquiries Prepare Resume, Cover Letter, Interview & Networking Activities to Explore Purposeful Work Professional Development Opportunities Mini Grant Funding Request Form Life After Bates Explore Job Shadow Program Self Assessments Industry Roadshows Spotlights on Alumni Career Paths Purposeful Work Unplugged Curriculum Practitioner-Taught Courses Purposeful Work Infusion Project Faculty Resources for Purposeful Work Infusion Courses Life Architecture Short Term Course First-Year Seminar: Purpose, Work, and College Opportunities Handshake Internship/Job Search Platform Purposeful Work Internships For Employers: Recruiting at Bates For Students: Recruiting at Bates Employer Recruitment Session Schedule Micro-Internships Grants, Credit & Fellowships Industry Specifics STEM and Pre-Health Support & Resources Pre-Law Support & Resources Pre-Business Support & Resources Pre-Engineering Support & Resources Discover Entrepreneurship Application Deadlines by Industry Graduate Support Graduate School Support & Resources Graduate/Professional School Events Outcomes Postgraduation Survey for Class of 2026 Class of 2024 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2023 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2022 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2021 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Preparing students for lives of meaningful work lies at the heart of the liberal arts mission. Purposeful Work at Bates is about helping students discover the joy and power that arise from aligning who they are with what they do. It helps students identify and cultivate their interests and strengths and provides opportunities for them to acquire the knowledge, experiences, and relationships necessary to pursue their aspirations with imagination and integrity. It is grounded in the Bates mission , has curricular and co-curricular aspects, and takes a four-year, developmental approach to working with students. Informed by this philosophy, students emerge from Bates equipped to make intentional decisions about their work, selves, and how the two relate. It’s about our liberal arts mission and an imperative in today’s world. What We Do is Unique. Here’s Why. Almost every college has programs or departments that help students find internships and provide career counseling. But Purposeful Work at Bates goes distinctly beyond jobs or careers. It has four key characteristics: It is mission-based. Our programming is built on the premise that preparing students for lives of meaningful work lies at the heart of the liberal arts mission. It is developmental in its approach. Our initiative encompasses cycles of exploration and reflection that integrate questions about work and meaning into the intellectual and personal growth that define the liberal arts experience. It is holistic. We focus on the whole person and weave concepts related to purposeful work into all aspects of the student experience: curricular, co-curricular, athletics, and residential life. It is highly intentional and pragmatic. We don’t just talk about work — we enable students to get deeply involved in work in its many forms. PW Quick Links Where We Are & Drop In Hours Schedule an Appointment Handshake RAIN Employer Info Session Schedule Cover Letter Guide Resume Guide Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authenticity, connection The Class of 2030, the third largest in Bates history, gathered to kick off AESOP on Friday, Aug. 28 — the day after move-in day. September 4, 2026 Opening Convocation at Bates welcomes Class of 2030, encourag… The college welcomed the Class of 2030 and new transfer students to the official start of the new academic year at the Sept.  1 Convocation on the Historic Quad. September 4, 2026 Bates welcomes (more) new faculty Bates News began introducing new faculty last week and will continue over the next few weeks. Read our second installment below. Bates\n\t\t\t\t\tCollege 2 Andrews Road Lewiston, Maine 04240 Phone: 1-207-786-6255 Make a Gift Campus Safety Communications Directory Employment Sexual Respect / Title\n\t\t\t\t\t\tIX A-Z Index Privacy Policy Questions &\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFeedback Virtual Tour Previous Next"
    },
    "https://www.bates.edu/purposeful-work/job-shadow/": {
      "title": "Center for Purposeful WorkOpportunities and Programs",
      "description": "Purposeful Work Job Shadow Program | Center for Purposeful Work | Bates College Menu Search Admission Visit Campus Visit Virtually Student Financial Services Academics Calendar Course Catalog Resources Campus Dining Menu Events Map Alumni Alumni Directory Events Reunion Arts Athletics New Students Library News Parents & Families Strategic Planning About Us Purposeful Work College Store Community-Engaged Learning Equity & Inclusion President Sustainability Support Bates The Quad Center for Purposeful Work Opportunities and Programs Page Menu Purpose Connect Where to Find Us Staff Team Make an Appointment Student Teams Purpose and Your Club PW Weekly Newsletters For Alumni and Parents In The News Media Professionals Media Inquiries Prepare Resume, Cover Letter, Interview & Networking Activities to Explore Purposeful Work Professional Development Opportunities Mini Grant Funding Request Form Life After Bates Explore Job Shadow Program Self Assessments Industry Roadshows Spotlights on Alumni Career Paths Purposeful Work Unplugged Curriculum Practitioner-Taught Courses Purposeful Work Infusion Project Faculty Resources for Purposeful Work Infusion Courses Life Architecture Short Term Course First-Year Seminar: Purpose, Work, and College Opportunities Handshake Internship/Job Search Platform Purposeful Work Internships For Employers: Recruiting at Bates For Students: Recruiting at Bates Employer Recruitment Session Schedule Micro-Internships Grants, Credit & Fellowships Industry Specifics STEM and Pre-Health Support & Resources Pre-Law Support & Resources Pre-Business Support & Resources Pre-Engineering Support & Resources Discover Entrepreneurship Application Deadlines by Industry Graduate Support Graduate School Support & Resources Graduate/Professional School Events Outcomes Postgraduation Survey for Class of 2026 Class of 2024 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2023 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2022 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2021 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Purposeful Work Job Shadow Program Mo Al-jabry ’29, Zach Louvat ’28, and Mary Parker ’28 shadowing Charis Loveland ’02 at Amazon Web Services in April 2025. Through the Purposeful Work Job Shadow Program, students connect with Bates alumni and parents to learn about professional options, personal perspectives, and how others have navigated pathways toward purposeful work. This is a smart first step in the exploration process, allowing students to test the waters in roles, industries, and organizations that might align with their interests and skills before committing to an internship, job, or advanced degree. The Purposeful Work Job Shadow Program also builds lasting bridges to professional contacts for Bates students, regardless of their inherited family networks, and creates important connections around work experience and identity. In 2026-27, the Purposeful Work Job Shadow Program will offer both virtual and in-person shadows . As such,  job shadow sponsors will have the option to design a shadow that is virtual, in-person, or either (depending on student’s location and availability to travel). Our complete list of 2026-27 Job Shadow Opportunities, will be viewable here in early October. Students from all four class years may apply for up to three job shadows each year. Shadows  take place anytime between December and the end of May. The job shadow experience will support the following goals for students: Explore and clarify potential career preferences Gain insight into a “day in the life” of a specific occupation and culture within an organization Identify skills and competencies needed to succeed in a particular job Develop contacts that may facilitate the search for internships and permanent employment opportunities The Purposeful Work Job Shadow Program, formerly known as CDIP or Career Discovery in Practice, has been connecting Bates students to alumni since 1978. Through the help of generous alumni and parents, we continue to evolve this signature exploration program. For Sponsors For Students Job Shadow Program Timeline September: Sponsors may register online until September 23, 2026. October: In mid-October, the Job Shadow Index will be published which includes links to Handshake descriptions for all shadows. Students submit applications via Handshake , following the Student Application Guide. A resume and statement of interest are required. Students must have a resume review by Purposeful Work before applying to shadows. November: Applications are due on Friday, November 13, 2026 at 11:59pm ET . See our Student Application Guide in Handshake for more information. December – May: In late November we review applications to make matches. Sponsors and students are notified of their matches in early December. Job shadows take place, as scheduled by student and sponsor any time between mid-December and the end of May. We suggest that sponsors and students refer to our guidelines when scheduling, planning, and preparing for their shadows. “I volunteered for this because I also took part in the Job Shadow Program while at Bates, and I wanted to give back. The [job shadow] I did really gave me a look into how that career worked day-to-day, and it was especially useful, because I was considering a field that does not offer internships. I really enjoyed meeting a fellow Batesie who was unsure of her future path, much like I was at that time…the feeling that you have helped someone, even in just a small way, to understand what they are meant to do, is a powerful one.” – Job Shadow Sponsor “It was great to meet with so many people, all in different positions…it allowed me a full understanding of the work that is done…and to ask a bunch of different questions. I left the office that afternoon with more information than I could remember!” – Job Shadow Student “I’m grateful for the thoughtful match and for the chance to connect with such bright and motivated individuals. I thoroughly enjoyed sharing my experiences running a dental practice and discussing both the challenges and rewards of a career in dentistry. During their visits, I also offered guidance on dental school applications and explored ways research and internship experiences can help strengthen their paths toward dental school.” – Job Shadow Sponsor “The day was spent meeting people from different teams and positions and understanding what motivated them to join the company. We had numerous opportunities to ask questions, gain insight into the startup environment, and receive advice on developing our career paths. Moreover, we even received all of their connections on LinkedIn to stay in touch for any further inquiries. Personally, this experience helped me reflect on what I want to aim for in the future and the kind of work I aspire to do.” – Job Shadow Student “The Purposeful Work program is a truly meaningful initiative that allows students to gain insight into real-world professions, clarify their goals, and build valuable mentoring relationships. I’m delighted to contribute to this effort and to support Bates students as they explore their futures in healthcare.” – Job Shadow Sponsor Examples of Past Job Shadow Sponsors Accenture –  Boston, MA A + E Television Networks – New York, NY Bigelow Laboratory – Boothbay, ME Bloomingdale’s – New York, NY Boston Children’s Hospital – Boston, MA CBS Productions – Los Angeles, CA Columbia Sportswear – Portland, OR Converse – Boston, MA Decision Economics, Inc. – New York, NY Department of State – Washington, D.C. ESPN – Bristol, CT EF Education First – Cambridge, MA Food52.com – New York, NY Genentech – San Francisco, CA Hope Animal Hospital – Brooklyn, NY Heywood Hospital – Gardner, MA IBM – Washington, D.C. ImmunoGen, Inc. – Waltham, MA JMA Ventures, LLC – San Francisco, CA John Snow, Inc. – Boston, MA Maine Coast Waldorf School – Freeport, ME Maine Office of the Attorney General – Augusta, ME Maine Red Claws – Portland, ME MaineToday Media, Inc. – Portland, ME Mercy Corps – Washington, D.C. Morning Glory Farm – Edgartown, MA National Aquarium – Baltimore, MD National Institutes of Health – Bethesda, MD National Safety Council – Itasca, IL NOAA Fisheries – Seattle, WA Plimoth Plantation – Plymouth, MA Ransom Consulting – Portsmouth, NH Rippleffect – Portland, ME Sports Illustrated – New York, NY TJX Companies – Framingham, MA Triumvirate Environmental – Somerville, MA UBS Financial Services – Boston, MA Under Armour – Baltimore, MD U.S. Attorney’s Office – Detroit, MI Questions? Contact us at jobshadow@bates.edu or 207-786-6232. Job Shadow Program Quick Links Student Application Guide Job Shadow Index 2025-26 Job Shadow Sponsor Guidelines Job Shadow Student Guidelines Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authenticity, connection The Class of 2030, the third largest in Bates history, gathered to kick off AESOP on Friday, Aug. 28 — the day after move-in day. September 4, 2026 Opening Convocation at Bates welcomes Class of 2030, encourag… The college welcomed the Class of 2030 and new transfer students to the official start of the new academic year at the Sept.  1 Convocation on the Historic Quad. September 4, 2026 Bates welcomes (more) new faculty Bates News began introducing new faculty last week and will continue over the next few weeks. Read our second installment below. Bates\n\t\t\t\t\tCollege 2 Andrews Road Lewiston, Maine 04240 Phone: 1-207-786-6255 Make a Gift Campus Safety Communications Directory Employment Sexual Respect / Title\n\t\t\t\t\t\tIX A-Z Index Privacy Policy Questions &\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFeedback Virtual Tour Previous Next"
